    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the area of a square given its perimeter, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Determine the side length of the square:**\n   - The formula for the perimeter \\( P \\) of a square is given by:\n     \\[\n     P = 4 \\times \\text{side length}\n     \\]\n   - We are given the perimeter \\( P = 32 \\) ft. So, we can set up the equation:\n     \\[\n     32 = 4 \\times \\text{side length}\n     \\]\n   - To find the side length, we divide both sides of the equation by 4:\n     \\[\n     \\text{side length} = \\frac{32}{4} = 8 \\text{ ft}\n     \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the area of the square:**\n   - The formula for the area \\( A \\) of a square is given by:\n     \\[\n     A = \\text{side length}^2\n     \\]\n   - We have already found that the side length is 8 ft. So, we square the side length:\n     \\[\n     A = 8^2 = 64 \\text{ square feet}\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the square is \\(\\boxed{64}\\) square feet.",
