    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the area of the square, we need to find the length of one of its sides first. Let's call the length of a side \"s\". The perimeter of a square is 4 times the length of a side, so we can write:\n\nPerimeter = 4s\n\nWe are given that the perimeter is 32 feet, so:\n\n32 = 4s\n\nTo find the length of one side, we can divide both sides of the equation by 4:\n\ns = 32 / 4\ns = 8 feet\n\nNow that we know the length of one side of the square, we can find the area. The area of a square is given by the formula:\n\nArea = s^2\n\nSubstituting the value of the side length we found:\n\nArea = 8^2\nArea = 64 square feet\n\nSo, the area of the square is \\boxed{64} square feet.",
